# trees — a click on an observed element folds its tree away, and another brings it back
#
# An observed element is the root of what was made of it: thoughts, acts, outcomes. A click on the
# element puts all of that away — the element alone is drawn, with a mark that there is more — and
# a second click brings it back. Folding is the screen's: nothing under the element is lost, but
# none of it is drawn and none of it answers a click while it is folded, so a waiting act cannot be
# carried out until its tree is unfolded again.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

strategy succeed
goal move
click observe "Test Field"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Field"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180

# --- unfolded: the element offers its fold, and its act waits ---
expect-state symbols click fold "the way to Test Field"
expect-no-state symbols click fold "the way to Test Field" (disabled)
expect-state symbols click act 0
expect-no-state trees folded=yes
point fold "Test Field"
wait
inspect pointer-label
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow
expect-state pointer-label · fold

# --- folded: the element alone, and nothing under it answers ---
click fold "Test Field"
expect-state trees element "the way to Test Field"
expect-state trees folded=yes
expect-state trees act state=waiting
expect-state symbols element "the way to Test Field" in "Test Yard" (folded)
expect-no-state symbols click act
expect-no-state symbols click think "the way to Test Field"
click act 0
expect-state where Test Yard
point fold "Test Field"
wait
expect-state pointer-label · unfold

# --- unfolded again: the act is where it was, and is carried out ---
click fold "Test Field"
expect-no-state trees folded=yes
expect-state symbols click act 0
click act 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Field
quit
